<p>Pakistan carried out air and ground strikes on targets in Afghanistan, including in Kabul, Kandahar and Paktia, after a sharp escalation in cross-border violence with Afghanistan’s Taliban authorities. Pakistani Defence Minister Khawaja Muhammad Asif said Pakistan’s “patience has run out” and called the situation “open war,” while Afghan officials said their forces launched retaliatory actions along the border after earlier Pakistani strikes. Both sides reported major casualties and battlefield gains, though many figures could not be independently verified in early reporting. Pakistan said the operation hit Taliban posts, headquarters and ammunition depots. Taliban spokesperson Zabihullah Mujahid said Pakistan struck areas in Kabul, Kandahar and Paktia, and said there were no casualties from those airstrikes. Explosions were reported in Kabul as the exchange of strikes continued. As the fighting widened, governments abroad urged restraint and a return to diplomacy—offering a narrow but real point of hope that international pressure and existing ceasefire efforts could still create space to step back from a broader conflict.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/lt4ycun09MKDPO7q4WjTal0gfn1smIj3ERJFQMfFvvK5MWix1XkpcgQrLtxEmLD7BhoMnywyF7h8n-ToYGPjX-y5oA05wwmRsgfddpT5hSeWVfJvSphvTArjYzxYjN_OwSQyv7bXVuZeiB4w-9Ywaat2nrvhn7uIn1lJ2dxyYmOJ-uLL1nXgwgXI-tDFfOKZROsGfnd215S7OiyZr_ETBZ1cCwDyRvE8txYySFDKhYyjaiowxE_u8hkJOxHLm1j5yxjN10VswdrCtq_3VQ' alt='A Pakistani army tank stands at the Pakistan-Afghanistan border in Chaman after overnight cross-border fighting.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Border sectors: Pakistan said Afghan fire and clashes broke out across multiple frontier sectors in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa—Chitral, Khyber, Mohmand, Kurram and Bajaur—and called its response “immediate and effective”.</li><li>Security posture: Firstpost reported Pakistan raised a nationwide security alert after it said Afghan forces opened fire at multiple border locations.</li><li>Casualty claims: Firstpost reported sharply different casualty figures, with Islamabad saying it killed 133 and Kabul claiming 55 Pakistani troops were killed.</li><li>Info war: NDTV and Firstpost flagged disputed online claims that Afghanistan downed a Pakistani F-16, while later reporting questioned the video’s authenticity.</li><li>Taliban tactics: Euronews reported Taliban forces described “large-scale offensive operations” along the border and claimed to have captured several Pakistani outposts.</li></ul><blockquote>Our cup of patience has overflowed. Now it is open war between us and you (Afghanistan), - Khawaja Muhammad Asif</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pakistan defence minister: Khawaja Muhammad Asif said Pakistan’s “patience” had run out and described the escalation as “open war” with Afghanistan. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/pakistan-open-war-afghanistan-pakistan-defence-minister-says'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Afghan Taliban spokesperson: Zabihullah Mujahid said Pakistani strikes hit areas in Kabul, Kandahar and Paktia, and said there were “no reported casualties,” while casting Taliban actions as retaliation. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/633102-pakistan-afghanistan-retaliatory-strikes/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Pakistan prime minister: Shehbaz Sharif warned Pakistan can “crush” aggressors as the fighting intensified. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/afghanistan-pakistan-war-pak-will-crush-aggressive-ambitions-shehbaz-sharif-warns-afghanistan-11143028#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Pakistan information minister: Attaullah Tarar rejected what he called “false and baseless propaganda” about the clashes, and said two Pakistani security personnel were killed and three were injured. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1975921/44-afghan-taliban-operatives-killed-2-pakistan-security-personnel-martyred-during-ongoing-border-clashes-attaullah-tarar'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>International community: Governments around the world urged both sides to show restraint as fighting erupted. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/27/world-reacts-to-eruption-of-fighting-between-pakistan-afghanistan'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/pakistan-says-it-is-in-open-war-with-afghanistan-launches-strikes-on-kabul/'>Pakistan says it is in &quot;open war&quot; with Afghanistan, launches strikes on Kabul</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/south-asia/article/3344796/pakistan-declares-open-war-afghan-taliban-after-morning-strikes-kabul-kandahar'>Pakistan declares ‘open war’ with Afghan Taliban after morning strikes on Kabul, Kandahar</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/02/pakistan-open-war-afghanistan-pakistan-defence-minister-says'>Pakistan in an open war with Afghanistan, Pakistan defence minister says</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/27/pakistan-declares-open-war-with-afghanistan-and-launches-strikes-on-kabul'>Pakistan declares &#x27;open war&#x27; with Afghanistan and launches strikes on Kabul</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/taliban-readies-suicide-squad-after-paks-bombs-target-afghan-cities-11143766#publisher=newsstand'>Taliban Readies &#x27;Suicide Squad&#x27; After Pak&#x27;s Bombs Target Afghan Cities</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-afghanistan-pakistan-kabul-attack-air-strikes/'>Pakistan’s defence minister says there is now ‘open war’ with Afghanistan</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/02/26/g-s1-111783/airstrikes-afghanistan-pakistan-war'>Pakistan&#x27;s defense minister says that there is now &#x27;open war&#x27; with Afghanistan after latest strikes</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/pakistan-afghanistan-attacks-dozens-dead-border-region/33689094.html'>Explosions Rock Kabul After Pakistan And Afghan